{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>was divided.</b> The languages were confounded and they were scattered from the valley and were dispersed throughout the world. We learn that Eber was a prophet, for he named his son after what was destined to happen. And we learned in Seder Olam that at the end of his days the division took place — for if you say at the beginning of his days, behold his brother Joktan was younger than he and begot several families before that, as it says ״וְיָקְטָן יָלַד״ and so on, and afterwards ״וַיְהִי כָל הָאָרֶץ״ and so on. And if you say in the middle of his days — Scripture does not come to obscure but to explain; thus you have learned that in the year of Peleg's death they were divided." "<b>And Joktan.</b> For he was humble and made himself small — therefore he merited to establish all those families."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:16.587863304Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}